    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d187">

                <pb facs="0201" n="197" sameAs="frus:frus1938v03/pg197"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/13238: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commander in Chief, United States Asiatic
                        Fleet</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Yarnell</hi>), <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Chief of Naval Operations</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Leahy</hi>)<anchor n="61" xml:id="d187-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-06-16T16:12:00+08:00">June 16, 1938—4:12
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 16—12:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>0016. Japanese source states that unless Chinese initiate peace talks soon after
                    fall Hankow Japs intend renew drive against armies at <pb facs="0202" n="198"
                        xml:id="pg198"/> once not repeating mistake of waiting allowing Chinese to
                    recover as after fall Nanking.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
